FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31302
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786659489
OL,3,CICE faces criticism as agents to be
OL,4,Cgiven electric shock gloves
OL,6,FThe announcement faced criticism on
OL,7,FWednesday from Democratic elected
OL,8,Fofficials and civil rights advocates,
OL,9,Fwho called it unnecessary and cruel.
OL,11,FThe devices, known as the G.L.O.V.E.,
OL,12,Fwhich stands for Generated Low Output
OL,13,FVoltage Emitter, are normal patrol
OL,14,Fgloves until an officer presses a
OL,15,Fbutton to activate its electrical mode.
OL,17,FThey must be applied directly to
OL,18,Fsomeone's skin to produce a voltage
OL,19,Fthat causes pain, which is intended to
OL,20,Fgain compliance from people who are
OL,21,Fresisting.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31303
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786659489
OL,3,CICE faces criticism as agents to be
OL,4,Cgiven electric shock gloves
OL,6,FUnlike Tasers, they do not leave burns
OL,7,For contact marks.
OL,9,FThe size of the purchase suggests ICE
OL,10,Fplans to give the device to most or
OL,11,Fall of its officers.
OL,13,FThe gloves have been used by local
OL,14,Fdepartments more often in jails than
OL,15,Fin the streets, where ICE officers
OL,16,Fhave increasingly used force to
OL,17,Fextract people from cars and faced
OL,18,Fprotests over their latest string of
OL,19,Fillegal immigration crackdowns.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31304
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786659489
OL,3,CICE faces criticism as agents to be
OL,4,Cgiven electric shock gloves
OL,6,FThe Department of Homeland Security,
OL,7,FICE's parent agency, issued a
OL,8,Fstatement that did not mention the
OL,9,Fproduct specifically or explain why it
OL,10,Fhad been chosen.
OL,12,F"ICE is constantly assessing the needs
OL,13,Fof our officers in the field to ensure
OL,14,Fthey have the tools and equipment
OL,15,Fnecessary to safely arrest and remove
OL,16,Fcriminal illegal aliens from our
OL,17,Fcountry," the statement said.
OL,26,@tD@AOUyD@IO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31305
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786659489
OL,3,CICE faces criticism as agents to be
OL,4,Cgiven electric shock gloves
OL,6,F"Every decision is made with careful
OL,7,Fconsideration and appropriately
OL,8,Freviewed to ensure that any technology
OL,9,FICE utilises is consistent with all
OL,10,Fapplicable law enforcement policies
OL,11,Fand standards."
OL,13,FSpeaking at a news conference on
OL,14,FWednesday, New York Attorney General
OL,15,FLetitia James said, "we are outraged",
OL,16,Fgoing on to warn that ICE officers who
OL,17,Fmisuse the gloves in her state could
OL,18,Fface criminal and civil consequences.
OL,26,@nD@AOUsD@OO]wD@UOUwD@eO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/11
