OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786659489
OL,3,CICE faces criticism as agents to be
OL,4,Cgiven electric shock gloves
OL,6,FWhile the devices are marketed as
OL,7,Fnonlethal and safe for the heart, a
OL,8,Fpending lawsuit alleges a 43-year-old
OL,9,Fman died in 2024 after he was shocked
OL,10,F27 times with the gloves and 13 more
OL,11,Ftimes by a Taser at a jail in
OL,12,FRichmond, Kentucky.
OL,14,FAn internal investigation found two of
OL,15,Fthe glove shocks lasted 45 and 99
OL,16,Fseconds apiece ` far more than the
OL,17,Fmanufacturer's recommended 15-second
OL,18,Flimit.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31308
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786659489
OL,3,CICE faces criticism as agents to be
OL,4,Cgiven electric shock gloves
OL,6,F"These actions not only inflicted
OL,7,Funnecessary pain but also heightened
OL,8,Fthe risk of serious health
OL,9,Fcomplications," the investigation by
OL,10,Fthe Madison County Detention Centre
OL,11,Ffound, according to court documents.
OL,13,FThe manufacturer warns the devices
OL,14,Fshould not be used against some
OL,15,Fpopulations that ICE agents routinely
OL,16,Fencounter: the elderly, small
OL,17,Fchildren, pregnant women and the
OL,18,Fseverely disabled.
OL,26,@nD@AOUqD@OO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31309
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786659489
OL,3,CICE faces criticism as agents to be
OL,4,Cgiven electric shock gloves
OL,6,FThe device's user manual also warns it
OL,7,Fshould not be used in response to
OL,8,Fverbal defiance, or for punishment,
OL,9,Ftorture or horseplay.
OL,11,F"It's too easy for this to get
OL,12,Fmisused, against a population that
OL,13,Fdoesn't pose a threat," former ICE
OL,14,Facting director John Sandweg said
OL,15,FWednesday in an interview on MS NOW.
OL,17,FThe maker of the Taser recently phased
OL,18,Fout its drive-stun feature, a similar
OL,19,Fpain compliance tool that had been
OL,20,Fmisused by some officers.
OL,26,@sD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31310
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786659489
OL,3,CICE faces criticism as agents to be
OL,4,Cgiven electric shock gloves
OL,6,FMichael Mannheimer, a law professor at
OL,7,FNorthern Kentucky University who has
OL,8,Fwritten about law enforcement and
OL,9,Fpolice use-of-force, agreed the gloves
OL,10,Fraised concerns about officers using
OL,11,Fdisproportionate force.
OL,13,F"One concern I would have is if ICE
OL,14,Fagents have this at their immediate
OL,15,Fdisposal, will they use it more than
OL,16,Fthey should?
OL,18,F"Will they jump over lesser force that
OL,19,Fcould be appropriate and successful to
OL,20,Fattain compliance and instead use this
OL,21,Ffirst?", he said.
OL,26,@uD@AOUzD@AOU}D@GO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/11
